From: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Jun 2024 17:09:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0956/1695] dts: stm32: declare RISAB instances as firewall
 controllers on stm32mp21

Declare RISABs as access controllers so that it's possible to check
firewall access rights on address ranges, and reconfigure dynamically
RISAB regions.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a7769e7940b7cbca401ca35f639a9ca1967eb29c dts: stm32: declare RISAB instances as firewall controllers on stm32mp21]
Change-Id: I8c2c51280ca3e604856549e5ee9ce643386e7d60
Signed-off-by: Gatien Chevallier <gatien.chevallier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/390285
Tested-by: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Gatien CHEVALLIER <gatien.chevallier@st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp211.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp211.dtsi b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp211.dtsi
index 74b8028c5..ce15a0dd9 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp211.dtsi
+++ b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp211.dtsi
@@ -562,6 +562,7 @@
 			reg = <0x420f0000 0x1000>;
 			clocks = <&rcc CK_ICN_LS_MCU>;
 			st,mem-map = <0xa000000 0x20000>;
+			#access-controller-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
 		risab2: risab@42100000 {
@@ -569,6 +570,7 @@
 			reg = <0x42100000 0x1000>;
 			clocks = <&rcc CK_ICN_LS_MCU>;
 			st,mem-map = <0xa020000 0x20000>;
+			#access-controller-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
 		risab3: risab@42110000 {
@@ -576,6 +578,7 @@
 			reg = <0x42110000 0x1000>;
 			clocks = <&rcc CK_ICN_LS_MCU>;
 			st,mem-map = <0x0a060000 0x10000>;
+			#access-controller-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
 		risab5: risab@42130000 {
@@ -583,6 +586,7 @@
 			reg = <0x42130000 0x1000>;
 			clocks = <&rcc CK_ICN_LS_MCU>;
 			st,mem-map = <0x0a040000 0x20000>;
+			#access-controller-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
 		bsec: efuse@44000000 {
